# Generated data for 2021-06-set1
SUBPARTS = [{'id': '2021-06-set1-conv-1', 'subpart_code': 'conv-1', 'section_id': '2021-06-set1-sec-a', 'section_title': 'Section A: Long Conversations', 'type': 'conversation', 'title': 'Conversation 1 · 离职面谈的倾诉利弊、职场流言风险与理性应对建议', 'topic_zh': '离职面谈的倾诉利弊、职场流言风险与理性应对建议', 'question_range': 'Q1 ~ Q4', 'questions': [1, 2, 3, 4], 'sp_start': 42.0, 'sp_end': 160.0, 'sentences': [('M', "It's my last day at work tomorrow.", '明天是我在当前公司的最后一天上班。'), ('M', 'I start my new job in two weeks.', '再过两周我就要入职新工作了。'), ('M', 'My human resources manager wants to conduct an interview with me before I leave.', '我们的人力资源部经理希望在离职前跟我做一次面谈。'), ('W', 'Ah, an exit interview. Are you looking forward to it?', '啊，是离职面谈呀。你对接下来的面谈抱有期待吗？'), ('M', "I'm not sure how I feel about it.", '我也说不好自己现在究竟是什么心情。'), ('M', "I resigned because I've been unhappy at that company for a long time, but I'm not sure if I should tell them how I really feel.", '我之所以辞职是因为我在那家公司过得不痛快很久了，但我拿不准是否该向他们吐露自己的真实感受。'), ('W', 'To my way of thinking, there are two main potential benefits that come from unleashing an agitated stream of truth during an exit interview.', '在我看来，在离职面谈中痛痛快快吐露真情实感，主要有两大潜在好处。'), ('W', 'The first is release.', '第一点是情绪的彻底释放。'), ('W', "Unburdening yourself of frustration and perhaps even anger to someone who isn't a friend or close colleague can be wonderfully freeing.", '向一个既非密友也非亲密同事的人倾吐内心的委屈挫败乃至愤怒，会让人感到无比解脱和释怀。'), ('M', 'And let me guess.', '让我来猜猜看第二点。'), ('M', "The second is that the criticism will, theoretically, help the organization I'm leaving to improve, making sure employees of the future are less likely to encounter what I did?", '第二点是，从理论上讲，这些批评能推动我即将离开的机构进行自我改进，确保未来的新员工不至于重蹈我的覆辙？'), ('W', "That's right.", '没错。'), ('W', "But the problem with the company improvement part is that very often it doesn't happen.", '但所谓促进公司改进的问题在于，这种愿景往往根本不会真正发生。'), ('W', "An exit interview is supposed to be private, but often isn't.", '离职面谈本应是私密保密的，但在现实中却常常并非如此。'), ('W', 'In my company, the information gained from these interviews is often not confidential, and the information is used as dirt against another manager, or can be traded among senior managers.', '在我们公司，从离职面谈中收集的信息往往毫无保密性可言，甚至会被用作攻讦另一位主管的黑料，或者在高管之间作为筹码私下交换。'), ('M', "Now, you've got me rethinking what I'll disclose in the interview.", '经你这么一说，我真得重新掂量在面谈中到底该讲些什么了。'), ('M', 'There is always the chance that it could affect my reputation and my ability to network in the industry.', '因为这完全有可能损害我个人的行业口碑以及日后在业内的人脉拓展能力。'), ('M', 'It is a pretty small industry, after all.', '毕竟这个行业圈子其实很小。'), ('W', 'Anything you initially gain from the instant satisfaction of telling it like it is, you might lose down the track by injuring your future career prospects.', '你在当下吐露实情所获得的短暂快感，很可能会因为日后职业前途受损而付出惨重代价。'), ('M', 'Right. Perhaps I would be better getting things off my chest by going to one of those rate-your-employer websites.', '你说得对。或许我真想吐吐槽、一吐为快的话，还不如去那种雇主点评网站上发泄一番。'), ('W', "You could. And don't do the interview at all. Exit interviews are not mandatory.", '确实可以这样。而且你甚至根本不必参加面谈，因为离职面谈从来就不是强制性的。')]}, {'id': '2021-06-set1-conv-2', 'subpart_code': 'conv-2', 'section_id': '2021-06-set1-sec-a', 'section_title': 'Section A: Long Conversations', 'type': 'conversation', 'title': 'Conversation 2 · 著名植物学家热带雨林科考纪录片背后的艰辛与飓风撤离', 'topic_zh': '著名植物学家热带雨林科考纪录片背后的艰辛与飓风撤离', 'question_range': 'Q5 ~ Q8', 'questions': [5, 6, 7, 8], 'sp_start': 240.0, 'sp_end': 375.0, 'sentences': [('M', "Today, I'm talking to the renowned botanist, Jane Forster.", '今天做客我们节目的是著名植物学家简·福斯特。'), ('W', 'Thank you for inviting me to join you on the show, Henry.', '谢谢你邀请我来参加节目，亨利。'), ('M', "Recently, Jane, you've become quite a celebrity.", '简，最近你可成了大红人。'), ('M', 'Since the release of your latest documentary, can you tell us a little about it?', '自从你最新的纪录片上映后反响热烈，能跟我们聊聊这部作品吗？'), ('W', 'Well, it follows my expedition to study the vegetation, indigenous to the rainforest in equatorial areas of Southeast Asia.', '嗯，这部纪录片记录了我深入东南亚赤道雨林考察研究当地原生热带植被的探险历程。'), ('M', 'You certainly get to travel to some very exotic locations.', '你确实经常能奔赴一些极具异域风情的秘境胜地。'), ('W', 'It was far from glamorous, to be honest.', '说实话，那里的实际境况跟风光旖旎、光鲜亮丽毫无关系。'), ('W', 'The area we visited was accessible only by canoe, and the living conditions in the hut were primitive to say the least.', '我们考察的区域只能乘坐独木舟才能到达，我们在棚屋里的居住条件充其量只能用简陋原始来形容。'), ('W', 'There was no electricity, and our water supply was a nearby stream.', '那里根本没有电力供应，日常饮用水全靠附近的一条小溪。'), ('M', 'How were the weather conditions while you were there?', '你们在那里的气候天气状况如何？'), ('W', 'The weather was not conducive to our work at all, since the humidity was almost unbearable.', '当地的天气对我们的野外科考工作极其不利，因为空气湿度几乎高到让人难以忍受。'), ('W', 'At midday, we stayed in the hut and did nothing. It was too humid to either work or sleep.', '正午时分，我们只能呆在棚屋里无所事事，潮热湿闷得让人根本无法工作，甚至连觉都睡不成。'), ('M', 'How long did your team spend in the jungle?', '你们科考队在雨林里呆了多久？'), ('W', 'Originally, we planned to be there for a month, but in the end we stayed for only two weeks.', '起初我们原计划在丛林里考察整整一个月，但最终我们只呆了短短两周。'), ('M', 'Why did you cut the expedition short?', '是什么原因让你们不得不提前结束科考行程呢？'), ('W', 'Halfway through the trip, we received news that a hurricane was approaching, and we had to evacuate at very short notice.', '行程进行到一半时，我们接到了飓风即将来袭的紧急警报，不得不匆忙接到通知后立刻撤离。'), ('M', 'That sounds like a fascinating anecdote.', '这听起来真是一段惊心动魄的探险轶事。'), ('W', 'It was frightening. The fastest evacuation route was through river rapids. We had to navigate them carrying all of our equipment.', '当时确实让人不寒而栗。最快捷的撤离通道是一处急流险滩，我们必须携带所有沉重的仪器设备在激流中穿行。'), ('M', 'So overall, was the journey unsuccessful?', '那么总体而言，这次科考算是一次无功而返的失败之旅吗？'), ('W', 'Absolutely not. We gathered a massive amount of data about the local plant life.', '绝对没有失败！我们收集到了关于当地热带植物生态的大量海量一手科学数据。'), ('M', 'Why do you put up with such adverse conditions?', '你究竟为什么能够忍受如此恶劣艰苦的环境？'), ('W', 'Botany is an obsession for me.', '植物学研究对我来说是一生的痴迷。'), ('W', 'Many of the destinations I visit have stunning scenery, and I get to meet a variety of people from all over the world.', '而且我涉足的许多目的地都拥有令人叹为观止的壮美景致，我还能结识来自世界各地形形色色的人。'), ('M', 'So where will your next destination be?', '那么你的下一站目的地会是哪里呢？'), ('W', "I haven't decided yet.", '我目前还没有确定好。'), ('M', 'Then we can leave it for another occasion. Thanks.', '那我们就留待下次有机会再细聊吧。非常感谢你的分享。')]}, {'id': '2021-06-set1-pass-1', 'subpart_code': 'pass-1', 'section_id': '2021-06-set1-sec-b', 'section_title': 'Section B: Passages', 'type': 'passage', 'title': 'Passage 1 · 科学传播中专业术语对大众理解与信任度的消极影响', 'topic_zh': '科学传播中专业术语对大众理解与信任度的消极影响', 'question_range': 'Q9 ~ Q11', 'questions': [9, 10, 11], 'sp_start': 475.0, 'sp_end': 608.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', 'Scientists often use specialized jargon terms while communicating with laymen.', '科学家在与门外汉或普通大众交流时，往往习惯性地使用晦涩高深的专业术语。'), ('Speaker', "Most of them don't realize the harmful effects of this practice.", '他们当中的大多数人根本没有意识到这种做法带来的负面不良后果。'), ('Speaker', 'In a new study, people exposed to jargon when reading about subjects like autonomous vehicles and surgical robots later said they were less interested in science than others who read about the same topics, but without the use of specialized terms.', '在一项最新实证研究中，那些在阅读自动驾驶汽车和手术机器人等前沿科技主题时接触到大量术语的受试者，随后表示对科学的兴趣明显低于阅读同类主题却通俗无术语文本的对照组。'), ('Speaker', 'They also felt less informed about science and less qualified to discuss science topics.', '他们同时觉得自己掌握的科学知识更匮乏，也更没有资格参与探讨相关科学议题。'), ('Speaker', "It's noteworthy that it made no difference if the jargon terms were defined in the text.", '值得注意的是，即使在正文中对这些专业行话术语进行了逐一释义，结果也毫无差别。'), ('Speaker', "Even when the terms were defined, readers still felt the same lack of engagement as readers who read jargon that wasn't explained.", '即便术语附带了定义，读者所感受到的疏离感与参与度匮乏，与那些阅读完全未经解释的术语的读者如出一辙。'), ('Speaker', 'The problem is that the mere presence of jargon sends a discouraging message to readers.', '症结就在于，专业行话术语的单单存在本身，就向读者传递了一种让人灰心丧气的心理暗示。'), ('Speaker', 'Hillary Shulman, the author of the study, asserts that specialized words are a signal.', '该研究的通讯作者希拉里·舒尔曼断言，专业术语本身就是一种强烈的身份排斥信号。'), ('Speaker', "Jargon tells people that the message isn't for them.", '行话无形中在告诉读者：这些信息根本就不是讲给你听的。'), ('Speaker', "There's an even darker side to how people react to jargon.", '公众对行业术语的心理反弹甚至还有更为阴暗严峻的一面。'), ('Speaker', 'In another study, researchers found that reading scientific articles containing jargon led people to doubt the actual science.', '在另一项相关研究中，科研人员发现，阅读充斥着艰深术语的科普文章竟然会导致大众对科学本身产生深刻怀疑。'), ('Speaker', 'They found the opposite when a text is easier to read.', '当科普文本通俗流畅、易于阅读时，情况则恰恰相反。'), ('Speaker', 'Then, people are more persuaded.', '读者在此时往往更容易被科学事实所说服接纳。'), ('Speaker', "Thus, it's important to communicate clearly when talking about complex science subjects.", '因此，在阐述复杂的科学命题时，做到深入浅出、表达通俗至关重要。'), ('Speaker', 'This is especially true with issues related to public health, like the safety of new medications and the benefits of vaccines.', '在涉及公众生命健康的公共卫生议题上尤其如此，例如新药的安全评价以及疫苗的防疫益处。'), ('Speaker', 'Shulman concedes that the use of jargon is appropriate with scientific audiences.', '舒尔曼坦承，在面向专业科研同行的学术会议或期刊上，使用行业术语无可厚非且十分必要。'), ('Speaker', 'But scientists who want to communicate with the general public need to modify their language.', '但那些渴望与广大社会公众建立有效沟通的科学家，必须彻底改造他们的表达方式。'), ('Speaker', 'They need to eliminate jargon.', '他们必须坚决摒弃和消灭专业行话。')]}, {'id': '2021-06-set1-pass-2', 'subpart_code': 'pass-2', 'section_id': '2021-06-set1-sec-b', 'section_title': 'Section B: Passages', 'type': 'passage', 'title': 'Passage 2 · 得克萨斯纺锤顶油田大喷发与现代石油工业钻探起源', 'topic_zh': '得克萨斯纺锤顶油田大喷发与现代石油工业钻探起源', 'question_range': 'Q12 ~ Q15', 'questions': [12, 13, 14, 15], 'sp_start': 670.0, 'sp_end': 818.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', 'At the beginning of the 20th century, on the Gulf Coast in the U.S. state of Texas, there was a hill where gas leakage was so noticeable that schoolboys would sometimes set the hill on fire.', '20世纪初，在美国得克萨斯州墨西哥湾沿岸有一座小山丘，那里的天然气泄漏极其明显，以至于当地的小学男童们有时甚至会点燃山丘取乐。'), ('Speaker', 'Pattillo Higgins, a disreputable local businessman, became convinced that there was oil below the gassy hill.', '当地一位声名狼藉的商人帕蒂洛·希金斯却坚信，这座冒着天然气的山丘地底下蕴藏着巨量石油。'), ('Speaker', "Oil wells weren't drilled back then; they were essentially dug.", '在那个年代，油井还并非像现代这样钻探出来的，而基本全凭人工挖掘。'), ('Speaker', "The sand under the hill defeated several attempts by Higgins' workers to make a proper hole.", '山丘地下松散流动的泥沙，数次击败了希金斯雇佣的工人们挖出合格井眼的努力。'), ('Speaker', 'Higgins had forecast oil at 1,000 feet, a totally made-up figure.', '希金斯曾信誓旦旦预言在地下1000英尺处必有石油，但这纯粹是他凭空捏造的数字。'), ('Speaker', 'Higgins subsequently hired a mining engineer, Captain Anthony Lucas.', '希金斯随后聘请了一位矿业工程师——安东尼·卢卡斯上尉。'), ('Speaker', 'After encountering several setbacks, Captain Lucas decided to use a drill, and his innovations created the modern oil drilling industry.', '在历经数次严重挫折之后，卢卡斯上尉果断决定采用机械旋转钻机，而他的技术创新直接奠定了现代石油钻探工业的基石。'), ('Speaker', "In January 1901, at 1,020 feet, almost precisely the depth predicted by Higgins' wild guess, the well roared and suddenly ejected mud and six tons of drilling pipe out of the ground, terrifying those present.", '1901年1月，当钻头探入1020英尺深处——几乎与希金斯的离奇臆测丝毫不差时，井口突然爆发出骇人咆哮，伴随着喷涌的泥浆，瞬间将六吨重的钻杆从地下轰出地面，将现场所有人吓得魂飞魄散。'), ('Speaker', 'For the next nine days until the well was capped, the well poured out more oil than all the wells in America combined.', '在随后直到该井被彻底封堵控制的整整九天里，这口油井喷涌而出的原油总量，竟然超过了当时全美国所有油井的总和！'), ('Speaker', 'In those days, Texas was almost entirely rural, with no large cities and practically no industry; cotton and beef were the foundation of the economy.', '在那个时代，得克萨斯州几乎全是一望无际的乡村，没有大型都会，工业更是近乎一片空白；棉花种植与肉牛养殖是该州经济的唯一命脉。'), ('Speaker', "Higgins' well changed that.", '希金斯的这口划时代油井彻底改写了得州的命运。'), ('Speaker', 'The boom made some prospectors millionaires, but the sudden surplus of petroleum was not entirely a blessing for Texas.', '随之而来的石油淘金狂潮让部分探矿投机客一夜暴富成为百万富翁，但暴增的过剩原油对得州而言却并非全然是福祉。'), ('Speaker', 'In the 1930s, prices crashed to the point that, in some parts of the country, oil was cheaper than water.', '到了20世纪30年代大萧条时期，油价暴跌崩溃，在全美某些地区，原油价格甚至比饮用水还要廉价。'), ('Speaker', 'That would become a familiar pattern of the boom-or-bust Texas economy.', '而这也自此成为了得克萨斯州经济大起大落、繁荣与萧条交替循环的经典典型宿命。')]}, {'id': '2021-06-set1-rec-1', 'subpart_code': 'rec-1', 'section_id': '2021-06-set1-sec-c', 'section_title': 'Section C: Recordings', 'type': 'recording', 'title': 'Recording 1 · 职场员工不满情绪调研：管理失当成因、有毒企业文化与资历陷阱', 'topic_zh': '职场员工不满情绪调研：管理失当成因、有毒企业文化与资历陷阱', 'question_range': 'Q16 ~ Q18', 'questions': [16, 17, 18], 'sp_start': 900.0, 'sp_end': 1092.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', 'Most people dislike their jobs.', '绝大多数人都不喜欢自己的工作。'), ('Speaker', "It's an astonishing but statistical fact.", '这是一个令人震惊但有确凿统计数据支撑的事实。'), ('Speaker', 'A primary cause of employee dissatisfaction according to fresh research is that many believe they have terrible managers.', '根据最新出炉的科研调查，导致员工深感不满的首要根源，在于很多人都认定自己的直接主管糟糕透顶。'), ('Speaker', 'Few describe their managers as malicious or manipulative though.', '不过，很少有人把自己的上司描述为存心恶毒或阴险操纵之人。'), ('Speaker', 'While those types certainly exist, they are a minority.', '尽管这类恶劣管理者的确存在，但他们毕竟只占极少数。'), ('Speaker', "The majority of managers, seemingly, just don't know any better.", '绝大多数主管表面上看来，仅仅是因为根本不知道如何科学管理而已。'), ('Speaker', "They're often emulating bad managers they've had in the past.", '他们往往只是在生搬硬套、模仿自己过去曾跟过的无能差劲主管。'), ('Speaker', "It's likely they've never read a management book or attended a management course.", '他们大概率一辈子从未翻阅过一本正规管理学书籍，也从未接受过任何管理培训课程。'), ('Speaker', 'They might not have even reflected on what good management looks like and how it would influence their own management style.', '他们甚至可能从未认真反思过什么是卓越的领导力，以及这该如何塑造自身的管理风格。'), ('Speaker', 'The researchers interviewed employees about their managers, beginning with a question about the worst manager they had ever had.', '研究人员围绕管理者议题对众多员工进行了深度访谈，开篇第一个问题便是聊聊他们职业生涯中遇到过的最差劲领导。'), ('Speaker', 'From this, the researchers came up with four main causes of why some managers are perceived as being simply awful at their jobs.', '基于调研反馈，研究人员归纳总结出了为何某些主管在工作中被公认为糟糕透顶的四大主因。'), ('Speaker', 'The first cause was company culture, which was seen by employees as enabling poor management practices.', '首当其冲的第一大诱因是企业文化，员工普遍认为正是病态的企业文化纵容默许了低劣的管理实践。'), ('Speaker', 'It was specifically stressful work environments, minimal training and a lack of accountability that were found to be the most blameworthy.', '具体而言，高压窒息的工作环境、近乎为零的岗位培训以及问责机制的缺失，被视为罪魁祸首。'), ('Speaker', "Often a manager's superiors can effectively encourage a manager's distasteful behavior when they fail to discipline the person's wrongdoings.", '很多时候，当下属主管做出令人反感的错误行径而高层领导却姑息纵容、不加惩处时，实际上起到了推波助澜的负面鼓励作用。'), ('Speaker', 'Such workplaces are sometimes described as toxic.', '此类充斥着不良作风的工作场所常被形容为“有毒的职场”。'), ('Speaker', "The second cause was attributed to the managers' characteristics.", '第二大诱因归结于管理者自身的人格性格缺陷。'), ('Speaker', 'Those deemed to be most destructive were odd people, those without drive, those who allow personal problems into the workplace and those with an unpleasant temperament or personality in general.', '被认为最具破坏力的是那些行为乖僻怪异、缺乏进取斗志、把私人生活矛盾带入工作场合，以及普遍脾气暴躁或性格恶劣的人。'), ('Speaker', 'The third cause of poor management was associated with a deficiency of qualifications.', '导致糟糕管理的第三大诱因与从业资质经验的严重欠缺有关。'), ('Speaker', 'Not so much the formal variety one obtains from a university, but the informal variety that comes from credible work experience and professional accomplishments.', '这主要并非指从大学取得的学历文凭，而是指来源于令人信服的实战履历与行业专业成就的非正式实践资质。'), ('Speaker', "The fourth cause concerned managers who've been promoted for reasons other than potential.", '第四大成因涉及那些并非凭借发展潜力与能力而获得晋升提拔的主管。'), ('Speaker', 'One reason in particular why these people had been promoted was that they had been around the longest.', '这些平庸者之所以能够步步高升，一个最典型的原因仅仅是因为他们“熬的时间最长、资历最老”。'), ('Speaker', "It wasn't their skillset or other merits that got them the job; it was their tenure.", '决定他们身居要职的根本不是卓越的技能或过人的功绩，而纯粹是其在职熬出来的资历工龄。'), ('Speaker', 'A point worth making is that the study was based only on the perspective of employees.', '值得着重指出的是，这项调研仅仅完全建立在普通基层员工的单向视角之上。'), ('Speaker', "The researchers didn't ask senior leaders what they thought of their frontline managers.", '科研人员并未向企业高层核心领袖征询他们对这些一线基层主管的真实评价。'), ('Speaker', "It's quite possible they're content with how the individuals they promoted are now performing, merrily ignorant of the damage they're actually causing, which might explain why, as the researchers conclude, those same middle managers are usually unaware that they are a bad manager.", '高管们很可能对自己提拔上来的主管业绩深感满意，完全沉浸在盲目自满中而对其造成的内部创伤一无所知；正如研究人员得出的结论，这恰恰解释了为什么那些中层主管往往从不自知自己其实是个极其失败差劲的领导。')]}, {'id': '2021-06-set1-rec-2', 'subpart_code': 'rec-2', 'section_id': '2021-06-set1-sec-c', 'section_title': 'Section C: Recordings', 'type': 'recording', 'title': 'Recording 2 · 西澳大利亚无人矿山自动化革命、新兴职业需求与偏远社区存续', 'topic_zh': '西澳大利亚无人矿山自动化革命、新兴职业需求与偏远社区存续', 'question_range': 'Q19 ~ Q21', 'questions': [19, 20, 21], 'sp_start': 1155.0, 'sp_end': 1338.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', 'With the use of driverless vehicles seemingly inevitable, mining companies in the vast Australian desert state of Western Australia are definitely taking the lead.', '随着无人驾驶工业车辆的普及已成大势所趋，坐落于澳大利亚西部广袤荒漠腹地的各大矿业巨头无疑走在了全球前列。'), ('Speaker', 'Iron ore is a key ingredient in steel making.', '铁矿石是现代炼钢产业不可或缺的核心原料。'), ('Speaker', 'The mining companies here produce almost 300 million tons of iron ore a year.', '这里的矿企年均开采产出高达近3亿吨的惊人铁矿石。'), ('Speaker', 'The 240 giant autonomous trucks in use in the Western Australian mines can weigh 400 tons fully loaded and travel at speeds of up to 60 kilometers per hour.', '西澳大利亚各大露天矿山投入运行的240辆巨型无人驾驶自动重卡，满载时重达400吨，行驶时速可达60公里。'), ('Speaker', 'They are a technological leap, transporting iron ore along routes which run for hundreds of kilometers from mines to their destinations.', '它们代表着矿业技术的巨大飞跃，沿着长达数百公里的崇山峻岭干线，将铁矿石源源不断运往目的地。'), ('Speaker', 'Here, when the truck arrives at its destination, staff in the operations center direct it precisely where to unload.', '当重卡抵达终点时，远程控制运营中心的工作人员会精准下达卸载矿料的操作指令。'), ('Speaker', 'Vast quantities of iron ore are then transported by autonomous trains to ocean ports.', '随后，海量铁矿石再由全自动无人驾驶重载货运火车直接转运至各大出海深水港口。'), ('Speaker', 'Advocates argue these automated vehicles will change mining forever.', '自动化拥护者们坚信，这些智能化自动驾驶装备将彻底颠覆并永久重塑全球采矿工业。'), ('Speaker', 'It may only be five years before the use of automation technology leads to a fully robotic mine.', '或许只需短短五年时间，自动化科技的全面渗透就将催生出首座完全实现机器人全自动作业的真正智慧矿山。'), ('Speaker', "A range of factors has pushed Western Australia's desert region to the lead of this automation revolution.", '一系列综合因素将西澳大利亚沙漠矿区推向了这场自动化工业革命的潮头。'), ('Speaker', 'These include the huge size of the mines, the scale of equipment, and the repetitive nature of some of the work.', '这包括矿体规模的极度浩大、开采装备的无比宏伟，以及诸多装运工序本身高度机械重复的本质。'), ('Speaker', "Then, there's the area's remoteness. At 502,000 square kilometers, it can sometimes make recruiting staff a challenge.", '其次是矿区极度的偏僻封闭——在这片广达50.2万平方公里的广袤无人荒漠上，招募足量基层工人往往是一项巨大的挑战。'), ('Speaker', 'Another consideration is the risks when humans interact with large machinery.', '另一大考量则是工人在现场与超大型重型机械高频近距离互动时所潜藏的重大安全风险。'), ('Speaker', 'There are also the financial imperatives.', '此外还有不可忽视的迫切财务经济考量。'), ('Speaker', 'The ongoing push by the mining corporations to be more productive and more efficient is another powerful driver in embracing automation technology.', '矿业集团对持续提高生产率与运营降本增效的极致追求，是拥抱自动化技术的另一大核心驱动力。'), ('Speaker', 'The concept of a fully autonomous mine is a bit of a misleading term, however.', '然而，“全自动无人矿山”的概念在某种程度上带有一定的误导性。'), ('Speaker', 'This is because the more technology is put into the field, the more people are needed to deploy, maintain, and improve it.', '因为现场部署的高端精密科技越多，其实反而需要越多的高技术人才去负责安装调试、检修维护与系统迭代优化。'), ('Speaker', 'The automation and digitization of the industry is creating a need for different jobs.', '整个采矿业的全面自动化与数字化转型，正在催生出截然不同的一大批全新岗位需求。'), ('Speaker', 'These include data scientists and engineers in automation and artificial intelligence.', '这其中包括数据科学家，以及自动化控制与人工智能前沿工程技术人员。'), ('Speaker', 'The mining companies claim automation and robotics present opportunities to make mining more sustainable and safer.', '矿业巨头宣称，自动化与机器人技术为实现采矿业的可持续集约化发展和安全本质化提供了前所未有的机遇。'), ('Speaker', 'Employees will be offered a career that is even more fulfilling and more rewarding.', '员工将得以从事成就感更高、职业回报更加丰厚的高端专业事业。'), ('Speaker', "Workers' unions have accepted the inevitability of the introduction of new technology, but they still have reservations about the rise of automation technology.", '劳工工会虽然无奈承认了引进新兴前沿技术的不可逆转必然性，但他们对全面自动化浪潮的迅猛推进依然持有极大的保留意见。'), ('Speaker', 'Their main concern is the potential impact on remote communities.', '工会最核心的担忧，是这场工业巨变对依附矿区生存的偏远社区所带来的毁灭性潜在冲击。'), ('Speaker', 'As automation spreads further, the question is how these remote communities will survive when the old jobs are eliminated, and this may well prove to be the most significant impact of robotic technology in many places around the world.', '随着自动化程度进一步加深，当传统的蓝领矿工饭碗被全面淘汰淘汰后，这些偏远荒漠聚落该如何继续维系生存？而这很可能会成为机器智能技术在全世界许多地区所面临的最严峻深刻现实拷问。')]}, {'id': '2021-06-set1-rec-3', 'subpart_code': 'rec-3', 'section_id': '2021-06-set1-sec-c', 'section_title': 'Section C: Recordings', 'type': 'recording', 'title': 'Recording 3 · 全球道路交通事故死亡率演变规律与交通法规执法的关键效用', 'topic_zh': '全球道路交通事故死亡率演变规律与交通法规执法的关键效用', 'question_range': 'Q22 ~ Q25', 'questions': [22, 23, 24, 25], 'sp_start': 1405.0, 'sp_end': 1602.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', "According to official statistics, Thailand's annual road death rate is almost double the global average.", '根据官方权威统计数据显示，泰国的年均交通事故致死率几乎是全球平均水平的两倍。'), ('Speaker', "Thai people know that their roads are dangerous, but they don't know this could easily be changed.", '泰国人民心知肚明自己国家的公路危机四伏，但他们却未曾意识到这种悲剧现状其实完全能够被轻易扭转。'), ('Speaker', 'Globally, road accidents kill more people every year than any infectious disease.', '在世界范围内，交通事故每年夺走的鲜活生命，甚至超过了任何一种致命传染病。'), ('Speaker', 'Researchers at the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation in America put the death toll in 2017 at 1.24 million.', '美国华盛顿大学健康指标与评估研究所的科研人员测算，仅2017年一年，全球死于车祸的人数就高达124万之巨。'), ('Speaker', 'According to the Institute, the overall number of deaths has been more or less static since the turn of the century, but that disguises a lot of changes in individual countries.', '据该研究所分析，虽然自世纪之交以来全球车祸死亡总人数大体保持平稳波动，但这却掩盖了不同国家之间剧烈分化的本质剧变。'), ('Speaker', 'In many poor countries, road accidents are killing more people than ever before.', '在许多极度贫困的国家，交通事故致死人数正创下历史新高。'), ('Speaker', 'Those countries have swelling, young populations, a fast-growing fleet of cars and motorbikes, and a limited supply of surgeons.', '这些国家面临着急剧膨胀的年轻人口、爆发式激增的私家汽车与摩托车保有量，以及极其匮乏短缺的外科急救创伤医疗资源。'), ('Speaker', 'It is impossible to know for sure because official statistics are so inadequate, but deaths are thought to have risen by 40% since 1990 in many low-income countries.', '由于官方事故统计数据严重缺失缺位，虽然很难精准核实，但在许多低收入发展中国家，车祸致死人数据估计自1990年以来已惊人地暴增了40%。'), ('Speaker', 'In many rich countries, by contrast, roads are becoming even safer.', '相比之下，在许多富裕的发达国家，公路交通正变得越来越安全。'), ('Speaker', 'In Estonia and Ireland, for example, the number of deaths has fallen by about two-thirds since the late 1990s.', '例如在爱沙尼亚和爱尔兰，自20世纪90年代末以来，交通事故伤亡人数已经锐减了大约整整三分之二。'), ('Speaker', "But the most important and intriguing changes are taking place in middle-income countries, which contain most of the world's people and have some of the most dangerous roads.", '然而最关键且引人入胜的重大转变，正在中等收入国家悄然上演——这里聚集着全球绝大多数人口，同时也分布着世界上最危险的部分公路。'), ('Speaker', 'According to researchers, in China and South Africa traffic deaths have been falling since 2000, and in India since 2012.', '科研数据显示，中国和南非的交通事故死亡人数自2000年起便呈现持续下行态势，印度自2012年起也迎来了拐点下降。'), ('Speaker', 'And the Philippines reached its peak four years ago.', '而菲律宾的交通事故伤亡峰值也在四年前成功见顶回落。'), ('Speaker', 'The question is whether Thailand can soon follow suit.', '现在的悬念是，泰国能否尽快迎头赶上这一积极潮流。'), ('Speaker', 'Rob McKinney, head of the International Road Assessment Program, says that all countries tend to go through three phases.', '国际道路评估项目负责人罗布·麦金尼指出，所有国家在交通安全进程中普遍经历三大演进阶段。'), ('Speaker', 'They begin with poor, slow roads.', '第一阶段起点于破旧、狭窄且车速极其缓慢的原始泥土公路。'), ('Speaker', 'In the second phase, as they grow wealthier, they pave the roads, allowing traffic to move faster and pushing up the death rate.', '在第二阶段，随着经济逐步富裕，各国大力推进沥青硬化道路建设，车流速度迅猛提升，但安全管控未能同步跟进，导致致死率急速飙升。'), ('Speaker', 'Lastly, in the third phase, countries act to make their roads safer.', '最后在第三阶段，国家痛定思痛、全面采取综合治理措施，强力保障公路安全。'), ('Speaker', 'The trick then is to reach the third stage sooner, by focusing earlier and more closely on fatal accidents.', '因此化解危机的诀窍，就在于更早、更聚焦地介入治理致命恶性交通事故，从而尽可能提前步入第三安全阶段。'), ('Speaker', 'How to do that?', '那么究竟该如何达成这一跨越呢？'), ('Speaker', 'The solution lies not just in better infrastructure, but in better social incentives.', '破局之道绝不仅仅在于修筑更平整坚固的硬件基建，而在于构建更强有力的社会激励与约束机制。'), ('Speaker', "Safe driving habits are practices which people know they should follow, but often don't.", '良好的安全驾驶习惯本是人尽皆知的常识法则，然而在日常驾驶中很多人往往明知故犯、视若无睹。'), ('Speaker', 'Dangerous driving is not a fixed cultural trait, as some imagine.', '危险鲁莽驾驶行为根本不是某些人主观臆断的“根深蒂固、无法改变的民族文化劣根性”。'), ('Speaker', 'People respond to incentives, such as traffic laws, that are actually enforced.', '人们始终是对切身相关的奖惩激励作出反应的——比如真正得到严格、公正、不折不扣严厉执行的交通法规。')]}]

QUESTIONS = {1: {'prompt': 'What do we learn about the man from the conversation?', 'options': {'A': 'He is going to leave his present job.', 'B': 'He is going to attend a job interview.', 'C': 'He will meet his new manager in two weeks.', 'D': 'He will tell the management how he really feels.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。男士在对话开头明确提到：“It's my last day at work tomorrow. I start my new job in two weeks.”明天是他最后一天上班，两周后将入职新工作，说明他即将离开目前的工作岗位。因此答案为 A)。"}, 2: {'prompt': 'What does the woman think about the information gained from an exit interview?', 'options': {'A': 'It should be carefully analyzed.', 'B': 'It should be kept private.', 'C': 'It can be quite useful to senior managers.', 'D': "It can improve interviewees' job prospects."}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。女士在谈及离职面谈时指出：“An exit interview is supposed to be private, but often isn't.”离职面谈本应当是保密私人的（It should be kept private）。因此答案为 B)。"}, 3: {'prompt': 'Why does the man want to rethink what he will say in the coming exit interview?', 'options': {'A': 'It may do harm to his fellow employees.', 'B': 'It may displease his immediate superiors.', 'C': 'It may adversely affect his future career prospects.', 'D': 'It may leave a negative impression on the interviewer.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。听完女士的警示后，男士表示：“There is always the chance that it could affect my reputation and my ability to network in the industry.”女士接着附和说这会损害未来的职业前景（injuring your future career prospects）。因此答案为 C)。'}, 4: {'prompt': 'What does the man think he had better do?', 'options': {'A': 'Pour out his frustrations on a rate-your-employer website.', 'B': 'Network with his close friends to find a better employer.', 'C': 'Do some practice for the exit interview.', 'D': 'Prepare a comprehensive exit report.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。男士在权衡利弊后提议：“Perhaps I would be better getting things off my chest by going to one of those rate-your-employer websites.”他认为不如去雇主评价网站上一吐为快、倾吐挫败与怨气。因此答案为 A)。'}, 5: {'prompt': 'What does the man want Jane Forster to talk about?', 'options': {'A': 'Her career as a botanist.', 'B': 'Her latest documentary.', 'C': 'Her month-long expedition.', 'D': 'Her unsuccessful journey.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。主持人亨利请植物学家福斯特聊聊她的作品：“Since the release of your latest documentary, can you tell us a little about it?”亨利希望她谈谈自己最新出版拍摄的纪录片。因此答案为 B)。'}, 6: {'prompt': 'Why does the woman describe her experience as far from glamorous?', 'options': {'A': 'She was caught in a hurricane.', 'B': 'She had to live like a vegetarian.', 'C': 'She suffered from water shortage.', 'D': 'She had to endure many hardships.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。女士坦言科考绝非光鲜体面：“The area we visited was accessible only by canoe, and the living conditions in the hut were primitive... no electricity... humidity was almost unbearable.”只能划独木舟、住无电简陋棚屋、忍受难耐的湿热，不得不承受诸多艰辛劳苦（endure many hardships）。因此答案为 D)。'}, 7: {'prompt': 'Why did the woman and those who went with her end their trip halfway?', 'options': {'A': 'They could no longer bear the humidity.', 'B': 'They had no more food in the canoe.', 'C': 'A flood was approaching.', 'D': 'A hurricane was coming.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。谈到行程为何缩短至两周时，女士解释：“Halfway through the trip, we received news that a hurricane was approaching, and we had to evacuate at very short notice.”行程过半时收到了飓风即将来袭的紧急消息。因此答案为 D)。'}, 8: {'prompt': 'What does the woman think of the journey?', 'options': {'A': 'It was memorable.', 'B': 'It was unbearable.', 'C': 'It was fruitful.', 'D': 'It was uneventful.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。面对主持人关于探险是否失败的提问，女士斩钉截铁回答：“Absolutely not. We gathered a massive amount of data about the local plant life.”他们搜集到了极为丰富的一手植物生态数据，说明科考收获颇丰、富有成果（fruitful）。因此答案为 C)。'}, 9: {'prompt': 'What does the passage say about the use of jargon terms by experts?', 'options': {'A': 'It ensures the accuracy of their arguments.', 'B': "It diminishes laymen's interest in science.", 'C': "It hurts laymen's dignity and self-esteem.", 'D': 'It makes their expressions more explicit.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。短文第二段指出实验发现：“people exposed to jargon... later said they were less interested in science than others who read about the same topics, but without the use of specialized terms.”接触术语的人对科学的兴趣明显降低（diminishes laymen's interest in science）。因此答案为 B)。"}, 10: {'prompt': 'What do researchers find about people reading scientific articles containing jargon terms?', 'options': {'A': 'They will see the complexity of science.', 'B': 'They feel great respect towards scientists.', 'C': 'They tend to disbelieve the actual science.', 'D': 'They can learn to communicate with scientists.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文揭示术语的负面影响：“reading scientific articles containing jargon led people to doubt the actual science.”阅读充斥术语的文章会导致人们怀疑真实的科学事实（disbelieve the actual science）。因此答案为 C)。'}, 11: {'prompt': 'What does Shulman suggest scientists do when communicating with the general public?', 'options': {'A': 'Explain all the jargon terms.', 'B': 'Do away with jargon terms.', 'C': 'Find appropriate topics.', 'D': 'Stimulate their interest.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文结尾处学者舒尔曼提出建议：“scientists who want to communicate with the general public need to modify their language. They need to eliminate jargon.”科学家与公众交流必须摒弃专业术语（eliminate/do away with jargon）。因此答案为 B)。'}, 12: {'prompt': 'What did Texas businessman Pattillo Higgins believe?', 'options': {'A': 'There were oil deposits below a local gassy hill.', 'B': 'The erupting gas might endanger local children.', 'C': 'There was oil leakage along the Gulf Coast.', 'D': 'The local gassy hill might start a huge fire.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文开头指出：“Pattillo Higgins, a disreputable local businessman, became convinced that there was oil below the gassy hill.”得州商人希金斯坚信冒着天然气的山丘地下埋藏着石油。因此答案为 A)。'}, 13: {'prompt': "What prevented Higgins' workers from digging a proper hole to get the oil?", 'options': {'A': 'The massive gas underground.', 'B': 'Their lack of the needed skill.', 'C': 'Their lack of suitable tools.', 'D': 'The sand under the hill.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。短文指出早期的挖掘困境：“The sand under the hill defeated several attempts by Higgins' workers to make a proper hole.”山丘地下的流沙屡屡击垮了工人们挖出正常井眼的尝试。因此答案为 D)。"}, 14: {'prompt': "What does the passage say about Captain Lucas' drilling method?", 'options': {'A': 'It was not as effective as he claimed.', 'B': 'It rendered many oil workers jobless.', 'C': 'It gave birth to the oil drilling industry.', 'D': 'It was not popularized until years later.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文介绍卢卡斯上尉的技术贡献：“Captain Lucas decided to use a drill, and his innovations created the modern oil drilling industry.”卢卡斯上尉采用机械钻机进行创新，开创了现代石油钻探工业。因此答案为 C)。'}, 15: {'prompt': "What do we learn about Texas' oil industry boom?", 'options': {'A': "It ruined the state's cotton and beef industries.", 'B': "It totally destroyed the state's rural landscape.", 'C': 'It resulted in an oil surplus all over the world.', 'D': "It radically transformed the state's economy."}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。短文后半部分指出，原本以棉花和肉牛为主、几无工业的得州，“Higgins' well changed that... That would become a familiar pattern of the boom-or-bust Texas economy.”石油井喷彻底改变了得州的经济形态与格局（radically transformed the state's economy）。因此答案为 D)。"}, 16: {'prompt': 'What is a primary cause of employee dissatisfaction according to recent research?', 'options': {'A': 'Insufficient motivation.', 'B': 'Tough regulations.', 'C': 'Unsuitable jobs.', 'D': 'Bad managers.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。讲话开头指出最新调研的核心发现：“A primary cause of employee dissatisfaction according to fresh research is that many believe they have terrible managers.”绝大多数员工将工作不满的主因归咎于糟糕的管理层主管（Bad managers）。因此答案为 D)。'}, 17: {'prompt': 'What is one of the causes for poor management practices?', 'options': {'A': 'Ineffective training.', 'B': 'Toxic company culture.', 'C': 'Overburdening of managers.', 'D': 'Lack of regular evaluation.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。讲话总结导致糟糕管理的第一大原因：“The first cause was company culture, which was seen by employees as enabling poor management practices... Such workplaces are sometimes described as toxic.”有毒的企业文化滋生纵容了糟糕的管理实践。因此答案为 B)。'}, 18: {'prompt': 'What do we learn about the study on job dissatisfaction?', 'options': {'A': 'It was based only on the perspective of employees.', 'B': 'It provided meaningful clues to solving the problem.', 'C': "It was conducted from frontline managers' point of view.", 'D': 'It collected feedback from both employers and employees.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。讲话后半部分强调该项研究的局限性：“A point worth making is that the study was based only on the perspective of employees. The researchers didn't ask senior leaders...”这项调研仅仅单纯建立在员工单向视角之上。因此答案为 A)。"}, 19: {'prompt': 'What does the passage say about the mining industry in Western Australia?', 'options': {'A': 'It is expanding at an accelerating speed.', 'B': 'It is bringing prosperity to the region.', 'C': 'It is yielding an unprecedented profit.', 'D': 'It is seeing an automation revolution.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': "【精析】细节推断题。讲话阐述西澳采矿业全面拥抱无人卡车与智慧矿山：“A range of factors has pushed Western Australia's desert region to the lead of this automation revolution.”西澳矿业正处于一场轰轰烈烈的自动化革命的前沿（seeing an automation revolution）。因此答案为 D)。"}, 20: {'prompt': 'What is the impact of the digitization of the mining industry?', 'options': {'A': 'It creates a lot of new jobs.', 'B': 'It exhausts resources sooner.', 'C': 'It causes conflicts between employers and employees.', 'D': 'It calls for the retraining of unskilled mining workers.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。讲话中分析矿山数字化与自动化的影响：“The automation and digitization of the industry is creating a need for different jobs. These include data scientists and engineers in automation and artificial intelligence.”自动化和数字化催生了针对数据科学家、AI工程师等大量不同新岗位的需求（creates a lot of new jobs）。因此答案为 A)。'}, 21: {'prompt': "What is the attitude of workers' unions towards the introduction of new technology?", 'options': {'A': 'They will wait to see its effect.', 'B': 'They welcome it with open arms.', 'C': 'They accept it with reservations.', 'D': 'They are strongly opposed to it.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。讲话在后半部分明确交代工会的态度：“Workers' unions have accepted the inevitability of the introduction of new technology, but they still have reservations about the rise of automation technology.”工会承认新技术的必然性，但抱有相当大的保留态度（accept it with reservations）。因此答案为 C)。"}, 22: {'prompt': 'What does the speaker say about traffic accidents in Thailand?', 'options': {'A': 'They have experienced a gradual decline since the year of 2017.', 'B': 'Their annual death rate is about twice that of the global average.', 'C': 'They kill more people than any infectious disease.', 'D': "Their cost to the nation's economy is incalculable."}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。讲话开篇指出：“According to official statistics, Thailand's annual road death rate is almost double the global average.”官方统计显示，泰国的年均交通事故死亡率几乎是全球平均水平的两倍（about twice that of the global average）。因此答案为 B)。"}, 23: {'prompt': "What do we learn from an American Institute's statistics regarding road deaths?", 'options': {'A': 'They are not as reliable as claimed.', 'B': 'They rise and fall from year to year.', 'C': "They don't reflect the changes in individual countries.", 'D': 'They show a difference between rich and poor nations.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。针对美国健康指标与评估研究所的全球死亡数据，讲话指出：“According to the Institute, the overall number of deaths has been more or less static since the turn of the century, but that disguises a lot of changes in individual countries.”全球大体平稳的数字掩盖了各主权国家内部巨大的分化变化（don't reflect the changes in individual countries）。因此答案为 C)。"}, 24: {'prompt': 'What is said about middle income countries?', 'options': {'A': 'Many of them are investing heavily in infrastructure.', 'B': 'Many of them have seen a decline in road-death rates.', 'C': 'Many of them are following the example set by Thailand.', 'D': 'Many of them have increasing numbers of cars on the road.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。讲话分析中等收入国家时指出：“According to researchers, in China and South Africa traffic deaths have been falling since 2000, and in India since 2012, and the Philippines reached its peak four years ago.”在中等收入国家中，许多国家的道路死亡率均呈现出显著的持续下降趋势（seen a decline in road-death rates）。因此答案为 B)。'}, 25: {'prompt': 'What else could be done to reduce fatal road accidents, in addition to safer roads?', 'options': {'A': 'Foster better driving behavior.', 'B': 'Abolish all outdated traffic rules.', 'C': 'Provide better training for drivers.', 'D': 'Impose heavier penalties on speeding.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。讲话结尾阐述治理之道：“The solution lies not just in better infrastructure, but in better social incentives. Safe driving habits are practices which people know they should follow... People respond to incentives, such as traffic laws, that are actually enforced.”除了道路硬件之外，关键在于通过严格执法培育更优的安全驾驶习惯与行为规范（Foster better driving behavior）。因此答案为 A)。'}}
